on its label. Bayer is seeking to settle tens of thousands of further cases.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Alexander Zverev clinches tennis No. 1 ranking</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff2dc02316bdab1e5582c709020d821ad29d9112632bfc396d6db6ce88e6fa81</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:03:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T22:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-alexander-zverev-clinches-tennis-no-1-ranking/a-79803048--1b03a09b61b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-alexander-zverev-clinches-tennis-no-1-ranking/a-79803048?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alexander Zverev is the second German man, after Boris Becker, to clinch the No. 1 spot in tennis.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Volkswagen logs Q3 operating loss of €5.86 billion on Porsche writedown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e14e79ded2949f101d4e45f53c3d8ae12662072fc9ef6d3382feb584725f713</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-logs-q3-operating-loss-of-_5-86-billion-on-porsche-writedown/a-79793796--74f8be5771cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-logs-q3-operating-loss-of-€5-86-billion-on-porsche-writedown/a-79793796?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Volkswagen Group has filed its worst quarterly performance since the height of the "Dieselgate" scandal in 2015. Share prices climbed in response, however, perhaps because the bad news was so well signposted.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Chancellor Friedrich Merz accuses North Korea of threatening Europe's freedom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:967de74fe89f4c566a45648f43b70bf0f73bdcec85c7c68310d912edb3982970</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-chancellor-friedrich-merz-accuses-north-korea-of-threatening-europe-s-freedom/live-79792915--91e1e32cf271.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-chancellor-friedrich-merz-accuses-north-korea-of-threatening-europe-s-freedom/live-79792915?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Friedrich Merz, who is visiting Seoul, said North Korea is putting Europe's security at risk by sending soldiers to fight for Russia in Ukraine. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Parties debate who should succeed President Steinmeier, with several women under discussion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9e28d7c1a49f23ee4a8f46e8c007f5ad20f0cf4fbe1ecd58f310427f4ee73a3</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parties-debate-who-should-succeed-president-steinmeier-with-several-women-under-discuss/live-79783779--1c6d43c0de10.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parties-debate-who-should-succeed-president-steinmeier-with-several-women-under-discussion/live-79783779?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's political parties are weighing possible successors to President Frank-Walter Steinmeier, with no candidate agreed yet. Meanwhile, a poll suggests most Germans are giving Halloween a miss this year.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany seeks new head of state</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58cd3ef5736ce8549653d2db45ccd8bd390764681cb68e6987d48e5c8301410c</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-seeks-new-head-of-state/a-79797794--10071c049ea1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-seeks-new-head-of-state/a-79797794?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The question of who should become Germany's new presiden is becoming pressing. Many want to see Germany's first female head of state. Chancellor Friedrich Merz is keeping his cards close to his chest.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich head coach Vincent Kompany's health scare highlights the need for better support for elite coaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b610c1c5f59b26d3fb7f720448710d82d901837e3349fa66e9c10a03ea29c84</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-head-coach-vincent-kompany-s-health-scare-highlights-the-need-for-better-support-for-e/a-79764661--fcbaed2aac2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-head-coach-vincent-kompany-s-health-scare-highlights-the-need-for-better-support-for-elite-coaches/a-79764661?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Vincent Kompany’s health concern is a reminder that elite football's pressures affect coaches too. Better support, clearer structures and mental health safeguards are increasingly vital.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Gen Z protests in Germany: Is France-style violence looming?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c399765452db1fd3744aa1a3f72ade754f98a810178eb2b48bd9147149200fa</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T13:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-in-germany-is-france-style-violence-looming/a-79788050--fb575275c7ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-in-germany-is-france-style-violence-looming/a-79788050?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Young people in Germany are preparing to protest over education and climate change. Politicians fear violence like in France, but an expert sees differences.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Can we regrow damaged seagrass meadows?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c15ec4a325fbaddc283ce00a69137b3cbe1ea32ca0161bb23903dff69cfeedd</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-we-regrow-damaged-seagrass-meadows/a-79617925--ee57fe9c850d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-we-regrow-damaged-seagrass-meadows/a-79617925?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seagrass protects coasts, shelters thousands of species and stores CO2. But some 30% of this valuable ecosystem has disappeared since the late 19th century. Can we bring it back?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Wagner brothers begin new NBA chapter on different paths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1c4a17104858ee9be801111eec1c5da027abd9daf4fc2dfb72f9d6edb16e75a</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668--ff5544415c4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After five years, brothers Franz and Moritz Wagner are no longer playing together for the Orlando Magic. In the new NBA season, their separation will likely mean the new "German" team is the Charlotte Hornets.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
